# BAWAAL ChallengeCam / UniversalCamera (LOCKED)

The **live camera viewfinder** and its interaction model are **production-final**. Do **not** restyle, reorder, or re-clutter these surfaces unless the user explicitly unlocks this rule.

## Locked files

- `UniversalCamera.tsx` (+ `components/UniversalCamera.tsx` re-export) — create FAB / SPARKS / JOSH / BATTLE hub camera
- `ChallengeCamRecorder.js` — Arena / Battles RESPOND ChallengeCam live view
- `PreviewScreen.tsx` — ChallengeCam **post-record** preview (speed / slow-mo only here)

## Live viewfinder contract (camera phase)

**Keep only:**
- Dark full-bleed viewfinder
- Top: Close / Cancel + clean title (mode or CHALLENGE CAM + challenge label)
- Bottom: Flip + **minimalist shutter** with **animated spinning dotted ring** around a **solid red center** (square/stop while recording)
- Native pinch-to-zoom on UniversalCamera (works while recording)
- Existing duration pill / BAWAAL Hub flows on UniversalCamera only (already shipped)

**Never re-add on the live camera:**
- Floating speed badges / speed chips / SPEED cycle buttons
- Slow-mo capture overlays or rails
- Flash toggle / torch chrome
- Zoom preset pills (1× / 2× / 3×)
- Extra text overlays, cluttered control clusters, or decorative badges

## Preview-only speed

- Speed options (**1× Normal**, **Slow-Mo**, Fast, etc.) live **exclusively** on `PreviewScreen.tsx` (ChallengeCam) or UniversalCamera’s post-record `ClipPreviewModal`.
- Do not move playback-rate / slow-mo controls onto the active lens.

## App wiring

- Stack `ChallengeCam` / `UniversalCamera` / `Challenge` → **`UniversalCamera` only** (Arena/Battles RESPOND included)
- Do **not** route Respond through `ChallengeScreen` / `ChallengeCamRecorder` (legacy)
- Preview speed controls remain on UniversalCamera’s post-record ClipPreviewModal
- Do not merge flash/speed chrome onto the live lens

## Allowed elsewhere

- Upload, persist, Arena feed playback, and non-UI logic behind these screens
- Critical crash/security fixes that must touch them: ask the user first and preserve this visual contract
